Creating a **lite version of Hearthstone** in **JavaScript** is a great project! Below is a **basic implementation** of the rules you provided. This is a **simplified version** that captures the core mechanics and logic, and it's **not fully optimized** for performance or game state management, but it's a good starting point.

---

### ✅ Features Implemented:

- 2 players
- 30 health, 0 mana initially
- 20 damage cards with mana costs
- Hand size of 3 initially
- Turn order and mana management
- Minions with health and damage
- Minion turn order and combat logic
- Game over conditions
- Basic card play and damage mechanics

---

### 🧠 Game Structure

We'll use **objects** to represent players, cards, and minions.

---

### 📦 Code

```javascript
// Game constants
const MAX_MINIONS = 3;
const MINION_HEALTH = 1;
const MINION_DAMAGE = 0;
const MAX_MANA = 10;
const MAX_HAND_SIZE = 3;
const MIN_MANA_COST = 1;
const MAX_MANA_COST = 10;

// Player class
class Player {
  constructor(name, mana = 0, health = 30, hand = []) {
    this.name = name;
    this.mana = mana;
    this.health = health;
    this.hand = hand;
    this.minions = [];
    this.turn = 0; // 0 for active, 1 for opponent
  }

  // Draw a card from the deck
  drawCard(deck) {
    if (deck.length === 0) return null;
    const card = deck.pop();
    this.hand.push(card);
    return card;
  }

  // Play a card
  playCard(card) {
    if (this.hand.length === 0) return false;
    if (this.mana < card.cost) return false;

    this.mana -= card.cost;
    this.hand.pop();
    this.minions.push(card);
    return true;
  }

  // Add a minion
  addMinion(card) {
    if (this.minions.length >= MAX_MINIONS) return false;
    this.minions.push(card);
    return true;
  }

  // Check if player can play a card
  canPlayCard() {
    return this.hand.length > 0 || this.mana >= 1;
  }
}

